WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:13.735
runKernel launches one warp of 32 threads. stride sets the distance between input indices, while output remains contiguous. n counts outputs; the input allocation must also cover the largest strided read.

00:00:13.735 --> 00:00:16.975
The host groups returned indices into sectors.

00:00:18.475 --> 00:00:19.965
Lane addresses.

00:00:19.965 --> 00:00:22.990
Each lane selects input[lane × stride].

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:24.515
Group addresses.

00:00:24.515 --> 00:00:27.185
Aligned sectors group the requested words.

00:00:27.185 --> 00:00:28.540
Return values.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.555
Each lane writes its contiguous output slot.

00:00:33.055 --> 00:00:36.630
One warp issues a load with an address for each active lane.

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:39.900
The memory path groups these addresses into requests.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:45.865
Caches may supply data before device memory is accessed; a sector count is not a count of DRAM reads.
